# Build context for the backend image (context is the repo root).
#
# The first entry is the important one: .env must never enter an image layer.
# Secrets are injected at runtime via env_file, so a key baked into a layer is
# a key that leaks with the image and survives every later "removal".

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Virtualenvs and caches — large, host-specific, and rebuilt in the image.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# The frontend has its own image and its own context.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Repo metadata the runtime has no use for.
.git
.github
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Local model caches; the image bakes its own.
**/.cache
**/models--*
